[Music]  this morning a london police officer who  protected u.s diplomats was sent to  prison for a murder that stunned the  british public  sarah everhard disappeared back in march  and was found dead a week later officer  wayne cousins pleaded guilty and now we  know exactly how he abducted her showing  his badge and then driving her away  holly williams is at the courthouse in  london with more on this story holly  this is so sad and upsetting to hear  good morning  good morning or the abduction rape and  murder of sarah everard by a serving  police officer in march touched a raw  nerve in this country angering women who  do not feel safe on their own streets  today in this court her killer was  sentenced to life in prison with no  parole the harshest punishment possible  in the united kingdom  sarah everard's brutal murder unleashed  an outpouring of grief from people who'd  never met her and a vigil near where she  disappeared when police tried to shut it  down citing covert regulations these  tactics added fuel to the fire  everard was walking home from a friend's  house down well-lit streets in central  london when a police officer falsely  arrested her kidnapped raped and  strangled her and burned her remains in  a forest do you know where it is  wayne cousins pleaded guilty but  originally told detectives he'd been  pressured into abducting a woman by a  criminal gang after getting into debt  and didn't know what they'd done with  sarah everard  and they said  they said you've done good  cousins was a diplomatic protection  officer whose last shift was outside the  u.s embassy he'd been accused on  multiple occasions of indecent exposure  but didn't lose his job  sarah everard was caring she was funny  she was clever said her mother in a  statement to the court calling her my  precious little girl in her last hour  she was faced with brutality and terror  i am haunted by the horror of it the  british government and police say  they're trying to make the streets safer  for women but this month an elementary  school teacher sabina nessa was murdered  as she walked to meet a friend her body  dumped in a nearby park  the the chair of the police federation  here said that sarah everard's killer  has brought disgrace to the uniform but  inside the court today sarah everard's  parents hugged police officers after the  sentence was handed down  nate  glad justice was served holly williams  in london thank you

